<Layout
  title={"Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade"}
  description={"About: Downward LUT6 compilation in a four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade, Yosys/Verilator xck26 RTL simulation, Split-Conformal ACI gating, and AirMoL 4-bit NVMe streaming on 2026 hybrid models."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study reports the public reference at openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai (commit d000c85). Backed by 27 six-kernel-verified Lean 4.36.0 theorems (plus 1,391 theorems across four OpenIE repositories inside Linux bwrap sandboxes, con-leche and con-ron --verified, zero sorryAx, CVE-2026-72844-hardened), it places a reconfigurable 6-input truth-table (LUT6) lookup tier ahead of Mamba-3 and 4-bit NVMe-streamed late-2026 hybrid and sparse-MoE models up to 120B parameters (LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, google/gemma-4-E2B-it, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B, Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct, Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, and nvidia/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B), gates commits behind deterministic verifiers, compiles certified wakes downward into clock-enable-gated 81-RAMB36E2 Beneš-routed lookup and canonical skill pages, and serves them over both Python and zero-Python single-binary Rust OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 servers (mol-agent / mol-agent-rs).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Physical DC shunt measured_j, 4-vendor GPU CubeCL parity, 120B, multi-repo SWE-bench, and reported_j results: six-host cross-silicon downward-compilation fleet benchmark anchored by Texas Instruments INA3221 (VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS) and INA238 (VIN) DC current shunts on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (Claim LA-24, board_metered = true: 3.74× Sub1Bit-LUT6, 34.21× Expert-AirMoL, and 10.94× Proposition 1 downward-compilation energy reductions with empirical break-even Delta T* = 0.108 &lt; 1 episode), single-source Rust Burn 0.22.1 / CubeCL INT4 Sparse-MoE &amp; GatedDeltaNet shaders verified across four GPU vendors (Claim LA-25: Apple Metal, AMD Radeon 8060S Vulkan [328.06× DeltaNet at 0.64 ms], NVIDIA RTX 4050 Vulkan [265.67×], and Intel Iris Xe Vulkan; &lt;= 1.8e-7 FP32 error), Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B in 970.0 MB = 1.47% FP16 RAM (12.30× NVMe cut), measured 120B-scale nvidia/Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B on Apple M5 Max (58,075.4 MB RSS at 22.17 tok/s; 62.50% verified pass vs. 43.75% standalone), BigCodeBench v0.1.3 (90.62%), 40 upstream SWE-bench Verified git-worktree evaluations across django, pytest, requests, and sympy (0.00% broken commits), and Rust mol-agent-rs (0.154 ms/req MCP, 17.21× faster; 38/38 pytest pass).</li>
        <li>RTL synthesis, CE-gated 4-stage 250 MHz pipelining, and VCD switching-activity audit: 41,185–41,623 xcup CLB LUTs in 1-cycle OOC and 41,465 CLB LUTs (35.40% of xck26) in the CE-gated 4-stage pipelined IOB-safe AXI4-Stream wrapper clai_benes_axi_stream_250mhz_top (reducing single-cycle logic depth 4.00× from 52 to 13 levels, fitting 170 &lt;= 189 IOBs, 81 RAMB36E2 blocks, 0 DSP48 slices, 320/320 CE parity, and 256/256 zero-bubble CPI = 1.00 Verilator parity), cutting AMD DS925 + Verilator VCD dynamic power 4.10× in quiescent idle (63.99 to 15.59 est_mW) and 2.69× during AXI4-Stream packet ingest (69.62 to 25.84 est_mW).</li>
        <li>Oracle-free wake gate: 0.00% false crystallization risk and 1.0000 OOD AUROC on the shifted test stream via a radially regularized JEPA-EBRM Split-Conformal + Adaptive Conformal Inference gate, keeping Conformal-bounded distinct from Deterministic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: physical Kria KV260 FPGA bitstream loading or KV260 rail power in this repository (measured_j = None across all xck26 FPGA rows; §4.22 and §4.25 switching figures are analytical est_j / est_mW excluding static leakage, while physical DC shunt measured_j belongs strictly to Jetson AGX Thor in Claim LA-24), commercial Vivado post-place-and-route 250 MHz timing closure, silicon energy leadership, or full 500-task SWE-bench Verified container evaluation beyond the 40 real upstream git-worktree evaluations across django, pytest, requests, and sympy.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
